Now I have everything. Here's the formal audit:

---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 / .NET 10 · **Integration-test calibration applied** (`[TestCategory("Integration")]` detected)

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 2 | 2 |
| Medium | 2 | 2 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell 1)

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)
**Integration calibration:** Not applicable — this smell is never acceptable regardless of test scope.

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

The `if/else` means only **one branch ever executes**. If the production code returns a `PremiumUser`, the name assertion is silently skipped — and vice versa. This is a hidden testing gap.

**Fix — split into two tests with explicit setup:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One entire behavioral branch is perpetually untested while CI reports green.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell 4)

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // No assertions — passes even if Insert silently drops every row
}
```

This test exercises code but verifies **nothing**. If `Insert` were a no-op, this test would still pass.

**Fix — assert the observable outcome:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage metrics show the bulk-insert path as tested, but no regression would ever be caught.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test (Smell 3)

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)
**Integration calibration:** Severity **downgraded from High → Medium** because this is a marked integration test. Timing waits are *more common* in integration contexts, but `Thread.Sleep` is still problematic because it's both slow (3 s per run) and non-deterministic.

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);

Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead of a fixed sleep:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5),
        interval: TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within the timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures under CI load; suite bloat — every 3 s sleep adds up.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Smell)

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);           // Which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);       // 4 assertions, 0 messages
```

Four assertions with **no descriptive messages**. When one fails in CI, the log says *"Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<…>"* — you must open the source to know which property was wrong.

**Fix — add assertion messages (MSTest 4.x):**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Persisted user should have a positive Id.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow diagnosis of CI failures; developers must context-switch to source code.

---

### Smells Scanned — No Findings (Clean)

The remaining 15 smells from the testsmells.org catalog were scanned and **no issues detected**:

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite is hermetic — not an external dependency |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods; multi-call patterns are appropriate for integration scope |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions follow immediately after adding that many items — self-documenting |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks in tests |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or skip attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No repeated identical assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests share `Insert`/`GetByEmail` but verify distinct behaviors |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Clean | Properly uses `[TestInitialize]`, not a constructor |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is descriptive |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB requires no external resource |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | No empty method bodies |

### Well-Written Tests Worth Noting

`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are solid: clear arrange-act-assert structure, focused scope, meaningful assertions, and appropriate integration-level complexity.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | 🟢 Low — add 2 lines | Eliminates false-pass risk immediately |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | 🟡 Medium — split into 2 tests | Closes a hidden coverage gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | 🟡 Medium — add poll helper | Reduces flakiness + saves 3 s/run |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | 🟢 Low — add message strings | Improves CI failure diagnostics |
